ype":"text"},{"text":"carrying an unrecognised value back into an update is refused by the server rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written as a spelling it never used. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over these cases needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":".unknown","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" arm.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"How a client proves its identity at the token endpoint (RFC 8705 §2, OIDC Core §9 naming).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Only the methods AXIAM actually implements are representable. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"None"},{"text":" — the public-client","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value — was deliberately absent until T21.2: adding it before the rest of the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"understood one would have let an operator register a client whose authentication is silently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"skipped. The server understands one now (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token.rs"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate_client_credential"},{"text":" has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an arm that accepts ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"no","type":"text"}]},{"text":" credential and refuses a presented one, the authorization endpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derives its PKCE requirement from this enum, and the admin API refuses the method alongside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any grant or binding that contradicts it), so the variant exists — and only that arm may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ever treat a missing credential as success.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientauthmethod"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections"